"""Fixtures for the Go gateway's Airframe tools (A-9 S5c), generated by driving the Python code.

What this writes:

  gateway/internal/backends/testdata/airframe.json   xr.request (github_pr.GitHubPRs.commit_xr over xr_request.build), airframe.apply
        (airframe_apply.apply over the resumable GitHubPRs adapter and glidepath-api) and the GitHubPRs methods apply calls
        (find_pr, pr_paths, repo_ready, onboarding_prs, read_file, ensure_pr), over canned upstream answers: each request (method,
        target, the headers that matter, the JSON body) and what the call returned, refused or raised. The Go test serves the same
        answers and requires the same result and the exact list of requests, case by case. A case may carry "go" (a different
        expectation for Go) with "why", and "go_requests": the exact requests Go makes where they differ from Python's (it reads the
        repository's default branch, checks that a branch is its own session's, reads the base before it writes, and works on a
        branch named with a part of the session). Both lists are written here from the same model of each call, and the model of
        Python's is asserted equal to what Python really sent.
  gateway/internal/airframe/contract.json, appspec.schema.json   copies of schemas/airframe-contract.json and schemas/appspec.schema.json
  gateway/internal/airframe/testdata/plan.json, state.json        from gen_gateway_airframe_plan.py and gen_gateway_airframe_state.py

Called by tools/gen_gateway_registry.py (outputs()), whose --check fails when a committed file differs.

    python tools/gen_gateway_airframe.py            write them
"""
